---
// src/components/Principles.astro
---
<section id="how">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head reveal">
      <span class="eyebrow">How I build</span>
      <h2>Engineering with a product owner's brain</h2>
      <p>Code is the easy part. The hard part is deciding what to build, why it matters, and knowing when it worked. Every project I take on runs through the same loop.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="principles">
      <div class="principle reveal">
        <span class="k">Problem</span>
        <h3>Start with the user, not the stack</h3>
        <p>Before a line of code, I map who's hurting, what they do today, and what "better" measurably means for them.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="principle reveal">
        <span class="k">System</span>
        <h3>Design for the second year</h3>
        <p>Clean domain boundaries, honest data models, and APIs that survive scope changes — so the product can grow without a rewrite.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="principle reveal">
        <span class="k">Ship</span>
        <h3>Production is the finish line</h3>
        <p>A demo isn't done. Done means deployed, monitored, handling real users and real edge cases — and boring to operate.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="principle reveal">
        <span class="k">Learn</span>
        <h3>Measure, then iterate</h3>
        <p>Every release comes with a question it should answer. Usage data and user feedback decide the next sprint, not opinion.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
